      "text": "# Original-shell classifier seam: narrow static review\n\nReviewed the concrete `autorouter/native_connected.py`,\n`experiments/native_connected_v1/driver.py`, its README and relevant authored\ntests, against existing `p.validate_candidate`, `p.transplant_fill`,\n`f.check_drc_stage`, shared publication, and schematic-field process evidence.\nThe project instructions were read completely earlier in this review chain.\n\nNo tests, Native, JVM, network, Git commands, dataset geometry inspection,\n`.runs` reads/writes, production edits, or subagents were used. Probe001's\nfailure and the lead's test results are lead-reported context, not independently\nreproduced observations by this reviewer. This excluded review directory is\non this Mac only; the lead owns checkpointing and actual probe002 execution.\n\n## Concrete seam assessment\n\n- The driver supplies the stripped task AST and its complete companion hashes to\n  existing `validate_candidate`. That helper saves/refills a separate copy,\n  transplants derived fill into the preserved shell, and runs a separate fresh\n  final DRC on the reconstructed candidate with schematic parity when supplied.\n- `nc.readback` checks the actual saved `refill-drc` stage against task hashes,\n  requires exact candidate bytes equal to `transplant_fill(task, saved_refill)`,\n  verifies the full candidate companion set, and checks the distinct unsaved\n  `final-drc` stage against that candidate hash. The shared checker requires the\n  actual parity argv and availability/field processes. Classification uses the\n  final report bytes, not a renamed saved-refill summary.\n- The strict task-versus-classifier-shell immutable and route equality remains.\n  A differently serialized saved native file is retained as intermediate\n  evidence; it does not replace the original task shell or its final report.\n- Repeated physical pads are admitted only within an identical native\n  reference/number/net group. One exact native alias is required per physical\n  copper pad. Real `@` identities, concatenated-token collisions, shifted/missing\n  aliases and cross-net membership refuse. Since activity is whole-net only,\n  same-net UUID-to-alias ordering need not be guessed. Native DSN process binding\n  remains mandatory. This is not a general alias or pad-geometry qualification.\n\nNo blocking original-invariant, final-report lineage, or whole-net alias-count\ncounterexample was found in this narrow static pass.\n\n## Finding fixed during review\n\n**NC-O1, P2 \u2014 Duplicate top-level witness fields were not checked.** Initially,\nchanging `native_witness`, `original_shell_sha256`, `task_native_report_sha256`,\nor `task_native` could make the display receipt disagree with the rederived\nclassification without failing `nc.readback`. The actual classification pins\nwere protected; this was a receipt-consistency defect rather than a proof of\ninvented connectivity. The lead added exact comparisons for all four fields\nat `native_connected.py:309`. These corrected lines were reread. Lead-owned\nintegration counterexamples should mutate/omit these fields against unchanged\nreal successful evidence, without rerunning Native merely to test the reader.\n\nThis review does not establish native eligibility, accepted routing, successful\ncancellation controls, a fair engine comparison, GUI support, improvement or\nphysical/electrical validity. The classifier-only driver remains\n`accepted=false`, with no engine. Future engine/central-receipt integration gates\nfrom the earlier review remain pending.\n"
